# The layers that deny the model's central claim, and the argument each one makes. One row per
# corpus layer filing the `absent` branch of `StatedRemainder`, beside how many corpus layers
# there are to deny it.
#
# The pair with the independence report
#   That pair is the point. This model makes two claims a document can refute in the model's own
#   format, and each has a wrapper built to carry the refusal. `Coupling` says the layers hold
#   their remainders independently, and the search beside it records whether anybody looked.
#   `StatedRemainder` says every layer has a remainder, and requiring the wrapper forces a sender
#   who disagrees to say so explicitly rather than leaving a field empty. One has never been
#   confirmed and has been contradicted. This is the other one.
#
# The rows need the second branch
#   They are visible only because `ingest.sql` reads the second branch. Read without it, a denial
#   arrives as five NULLs, with sign, absorber and quantity all blank, which is exactly the shape
#   of a document that said nothing. `refutation/object-storage` anticipated that in its own note:
#   "filed as a counter-example to the claim that every layer carries a remainder, not as a gap in
#   this document". An ingest that read only the first branch once stored exactly that gap.
#
# Corpus only
#   On the same argument as the independence report. "The model has been contradicted" is a claim
#   about the evidence. A fixture that denies a remainder proves the branch works and says nothing
#   whatever about the world, so counting one here would manufacture a refutation nobody made.
-- pm:StatedRemainder's absent branch, over the corpus.
SELECT d.filing, d.layer, d.reason,
       regexp_replace(d.argument, '\s+', ' ', 'g') AS the_counter_example,
       format('%s of %s corpus layers deny having one',
              count(*) OVER (),
              (SELECT count(*) FROM (
                    :compose(layers/every_layer.sqlc)
                ) l
                JOIN (
                    :compose(scope/corpus.sqlc)
                ) sc USING (filing))) AS how_common
FROM (
    :compose(layers/denied_remainders.sqlc)
) d
JOIN (
    :compose(scope/corpus.sqlc)
) s USING (filing)
ORDER BY d.filing, d.layer
